Nice, but I think it's confusing the issue to list non-default
behaviors--for instance, 'j' normally moves down in a default setup.
Listing it as jump is confusing to a new player, since it won't work
unless they fiddle the setup and turn on the weird number_pad option
(which breaks the regular motion keys). I'd just list "#jump" to jump,
since that's the default setting.

Either that or I'd make seperate cards for normal behavior and
number_pad behavior (with a big heading at the top of number_pad
explaining that it's not default and how to turn on the option).  But
personally I think it's enough just to go with the defaults; if people
start mucking with options, they probably have more of an idea what
they're doing.



